    "summary": "quie is a dark pool for tokenized stocks. it replaces the visible order book with sealed rounds.\n\nhow it works: you commit a hash of your order (side, size, price band, salt) and escrow funds. the chain records only the commitment. at round close, orders open to a threshold committee and eligible orders cross pro-rata at the public midpoint. everyone in a round gets the same price. one round later, the fill is tolled on-chain.\n\nwhat this means: nothing about your order is readable before it fills. an order that doesn't fill is never published. speed buys nothing, because first and last in a round get the same fill.\n\nwhat it doesn't do: you get the mid, not better. escrow size and timing leak an upper bound. the committee sees orders for one round, and that exposure is logged. the full list of what leaks is public on our site.\n\ndevnet is live with TSLAx, SPYx and NVDAx. next: Robinhood Chain.\n\nno book. no queue. only the toll.",
